New version on the cheat sheets page:
http://www.lojban.org/tiki/tiki-index.php?page=jbo_cheat_sheet

I've posted three versions:  1 page (for example to print it A0 and
hang on your wall :) ), 2 pages (front back landscape) and 4 pages
(possibly to print as a booklet).

I've checked and it seems I've no control over the mime/type of wiki
attachements. Does any one else has problems while opening PDF files?

About {ze'ei}, jbovlaste says that it works like {zei} but has the
grammar of the right valsi and the semantic of the first. Not sure how
it is supposed to be used.

The other experimental cmavo seems very reasonable (especially
{fu'au}). I have some reserve for the "replacement" cmavo but I don't
like {si} and friends too, so I might be biased.

Hope you find it of some help.

As always the OpenOffice files are attached for those wanting to
add/change them.

Remo.

